# K components

## Layers (do not collapse)

```text
useKQuery          → resolve list view + server fetch (page, q, domain, groupBy)
KQueryShell        → KSearch + KPagination + loading/empty
KTableView / KKanbanBoard  → presentational only
KTable / KKanban / KCollection  → conveniences on top
```

- **Fetch** model/CQRS lists only via **`useKQuery`**. Do not call `listModelRecordsPage` from views unless building a custom adapter.
- **Server-side** pagination/search when `paginated` / `searchable` are set — no client `sliceItems` in query mode.
- Chrome flags: `paginated` / `searchable` as `true` or config (`url`, `pageSize`, field allowlists, …).

## Prefer query props

```tsx
// ✅
<KTable query="hellospec.greetings" paginated searchable />
<KKanban query="…" paginated searchable groupByField="mood" card={…} />
<KCollection query="…" paginated searchable groupByField="status" card={…} />

// ❌ items + hand-rolled fetch for normal models
// ❌ DataTable inside KCollection query mode (use KTableView)
// ❌ Client search UI when searchable / KSearch applies
```

## Escape hatch

`items` (+ optional client filter/page) only for **non-CQRS** data. Prefer virtual model + `RegisterModel` (see appman) so `query="app.list"` still works.

## Forms

- `KForm` + `KFormField` with `command` or `model` — same CQRS resolve pattern.
- Refresh sibling tables via `refreshToken` after successful create.

## Hotkeys

`KSearch` / `KPagination` / `KForm` expose stable `data-keymap-id`s; bindings live in `apps/core/keymap.yaml`. Extend via keymap (see `.cursor/rules/keymap.mdc`) — do not add local `keydown` handlers for list chrome.

## Imports

Export/consume from `@/k`. Shared types: `KQueryPaginationConfig`, `KQuerySearchConfig`.
